{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And the kings of… five of…</b> The reason the verse needed to mention their number is to say that they were killed together, this one with that one, and they saw one another in their downfall. And its saying <b>the kings of Midian</b> a second time — perhaps the repetition intends to say that they killed them with full awareness that they were the kings of Midian, and not absent-mindedly:" "<b>They killed with the sword.</b> It was necessary to say <b>they killed</b>, even though it is understood that they killed him from the proximity of his mention with those who were killed. It is explained according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Sifrei) who said that Bilaam went from Midian to meet Israel to advise them so that they would not wage war against Midian, and he said to them: ״And what when you were…״ and so on. These words indicate that Bilaam was killed before the killing of the five kings of Midian, and this is what the verse was precise about and singled out for him a killing of his own, to inform you that he was not killed together with them — which would not have been understood had it not said ״they killed.״ And its saying <b>with the sword</b> is to say that they nullified his sorceries through Israel's spiritual counterpart and killed him physically."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:08.469299808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}